{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/873199-attack-of-the-cicadas","id":873199,"title":"Attack of the Cicadas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-24T11:42:54-07:00","id":873199,"title":"Attack of the Cicadas","content":"I'm talking about <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/morning-mix/wp/2016/04/15/billions-of-cicadas-will-descend-upon-the-northeastern-united-states-as-another-17-year-cycle-conclude/\" target=\"_blank\">this</a><br /> <br /> While the Cicada Host was presented as a Japanese, we do have Spider and Rat Hosts all around the world- so why not? Even if only one percent of those Cicadas are actually Shards, it would still create a sudden rise in the population of that Host, which could end up as a major change in the local spiritual ecosystem. Perhaps the Hunter in the Darkness where those awakenings happen wait for those events in advance, engaging their own, great &quot;cicada hunt&quot; when the time comes every 13 or 17 years? What kind of states and Dead Powers would you give to that Host?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T14:23:22-07:00","id":873280,"title":"","content":"Perhaps like the cicada themselves, a long term symbiosis. A shard burrows into a person or Gauntlet but remains undetectable as it merges until it suddenly awakens and takes over at some supernatural cue. They apparently drink the juice of trees, you could probably attribute some vampiric drinking to them if you really wanted.<br /> <br /> And of course the droning would have strange powers, driving people to varying degrees of insanity or action, forcing them to sleep, making passage through the Gauntlet a maddening procedure as it's full of chaotic sounds echoing and bouncing back and forth in the limited void.<br /> <br /> You might tie something in with tinnitus if you want to stick with the sound stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T14:30:28-07:00","id":873287,"title":"","content":"Some kind of maddening or disorienting sound effect would definitely be a good idea, I think. I would think that the cicada hosts themselves would be relatively benevolent, compared to the Azlu and Beshilu, considering that real cicadas don't really pose any direct threat to anything else. They would probably have to be more of a 'danger by existence' kind of thing. They're not actively malicious, but their presence has its own problems. Maybe their sound drives spirits around them mad. What if the pack's totem is affected?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T08:52:20-07:00","id":873793,"title":"","content":"Lots of sound based dread powers, and perhaps something to do with shedding one's skin to reduce damage/heal/resurrect from death ( you know, so you don't have to either A) find a new host or B), go back into the Gauntlet for however many months/ years). Oh! because Cicadas are connected to the summer months.,. why not give them an ability to manipulate heat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T14:19:30-07:00","id":874017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/873199-attack-of-the-cicadas?p=873793#post873793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lots of sound based dread powers, and perhaps something to do with shedding one's skin to reduce damage/heal/resurrect from death ( you know, so you don't have to either A) find a new host or B), go back into the Gauntlet for however many months/ years). Oh! because Cicadas are connected to the summer months.,. why not give them an ability to manipulate heat?</div> </div> </div> </div>With the heat manipulation, it reminds me of something that some bees do to fight off intruders in the hive without having to sting them. They grab onto the intruder, enclosing it in a ball of bees. The bees then start to vibrate their wings, heating up the air and effectively cooking the intruder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T15:44:33-07:00","id":874074,"title":"","content":"The cicada-hosts appear, seemingly at random, from time to time. They come in swarms, then disappear. A few Uratha have noticed that the swarms appear after intervals of 13 and 17 years and that the different sub-species are subtly different. The 17-year strain are especially nasty, simply because they appear so infrequently.<br /> <br /> This could combine well with the 'dormant infection' idea nofather suggested.<br /> <br /> Korogra, the shin-shedding thing ties into their role in Chinese mythology. Maybe they're very good at faking their deaths, even by Host standards.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":452,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","user":"Eremite","date":". 04-25-2016, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T17:32:44-07:00","id":874124,"title":"","content":"Part of my problem with the hosts is that their motivation is so basic. I love them as antagonists, they got body horror and numbers, they're infiltrators and can be a variety of sizes and shapes. But when it comes down to it it seems to boil down to, 'Do something to the Gauntlet.' And it's instinctual, I get it, they're working off of some belief even they don't understand, and there's rumors about why they do it, and it's certainly bad for humanity. But it seems like if there was a solid answer for <i>why </i>there would be more to work with. Is it going to recreate their Pangaean progenitor? Are they making the conditions for one of whatever their version of a Firstborn to come across and lead them? Do they need it to combine into a particularly massive host? Or are they 'just' screwing with the Gauntlet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T17:51:18-07:00","id":874132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/873199-attack-of-the-cicadas?p=874124#post874124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of my problem with the hosts is that their motivation is so basic. I love them as antagonists, they got body horror and numbers, they're infiltrators and can be a variety of sizes and shapes. But when it comes down to it it seems to boil down to, 'Do something to the Gauntlet.' And it's instinctual, I get it, they're working off of some belief even they don't understand, and there's rumors about why they do it, and it's certainly bad for humanity. But it seems like if there was a solid answer for <i>why </i>there would be more to work with. Is it going to recreate their Pangaean progenitor? Are they making the conditions for one of whatever their version of a Firstborn to come across and lead them? Do they need it to combine into a particularly massive host? Or are they 'just' screwing with the Gauntlet?</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I've heard about Dark Eras and the death of Wolf, the Gauntlet seems to be Pangaea shrunk to the size of a dimensional membrane, Wolf's last attempt at separating Flesh from Shadow. I'm pretty much convinced that the Hosts know Wolf might return if Pangaea is recreated, so instinctually destroying the pseudo-remains of Wolf makes a lot of sense, like maggots eating the rotten carcass of their greatest enemy.<br /> <br /> As Hosts grow in power, though, I believe their motivation switch from &quot;Gauntlet messing&quot; to reforming into the great progenitor. They gain intellect and power, and start to understand what they can become and who is their real threat here in this new world: Uratha.<br /> <br /> However, I do agree that Hosts are too &quot;Black and White&quot; antagonists, beings of utter evil that leave little for interpretation. They overlap too much with Spirits, in my view, just a little harder to detect and less prone to become allies. I would like to see an expansion to Hosts, allowing them more complexity, something that really gives you a reason to struggle with the need to eradicate them.<br /> <br /> My two cents on the Cicada: Love the Heat and Sound idea, and maybe you could move them to a shade of grey antagonism, with them being useful to the Hisil ecosystem somehow. Maybe beings that spend millenia asleep under the earth, having to emerge to devour, but also possessing rare knowledge of Rituals or even Gifts that might aid the Uratha. They might have no grudge against Wolf, and be a neutral Host that may, or may not, fuck up your life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5446,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","user":"BinAly","date":". 04-25-2016, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T20:20:44-07:00","id":874223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/873199-attack-of-the-cicadas?p=874124#post874124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of my problem with the hosts is that their motivation is so basic. I love them as antagonists, they got body horror and numbers, they're infiltrators and can be a variety of sizes and shapes. But when it comes down to it it seems to boil down to, 'Do something to the Gauntlet.' And it's instinctual, I get it, they're working off of some belief even they don't understand, and there's rumors about why they do it, and it's certainly bad for humanity. But it seems like if there was a solid answer for <i>why </i>there would be more to work with. Is it going to recreate their Pangaean progenitor? Are they making the conditions for one of whatever their version of a Firstborn to come across and lead them? Do they need it to combine into a particularly massive host? Or are they 'just' screwing with the Gauntlet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, simple motivations work all fine and good for say Xenomorphs, but merging with humans along their evolution do give them more nuance. Look at the Parlor Games SAS for example. The Leatherworker was savvy enough to manage a criminal enterprise. The Eye-Eater on the other end of the spectrum, prefers inhabiting hosts particularly close to Uratha and sabotaging them before they realize their human packmate is working against them, and isn't even motivated to weaving on the Gauntlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T06:40:33-07:00","id":874497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/873199-attack-of-the-cicadas?p=874074#post874074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The cicada-hosts appear, seemingly at random, from time to time. They come in swarms, then disappear. A few Uratha have noticed that the swarms appear after intervals of 13 and 17 years and that the different sub-species are subtly different. The 17-year strain are especially nasty, simply because they appear so infrequently.<br /> <br /> This could combine well with the 'dormant infection' idea nofather suggested.<br /> <br /> Korogra, the shin-shedding thing ties into their role in Chinese mythology. Maybe they're very good at faking their deaths, even by Host standards.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Holy shit, shin shedding sounds even more terrifying than skin shedding D:<br /> <br /> Joking aside, that's why I mentioned it :3<br /> <br /> I am always for ways for making Hosts harder to destroy, so using some sort of skin-shedding technique is just a natural conclusion, mythological tie ins are a nice bonus for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T06:51:47-07:00","id":874501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/873199-attack-of-the-cicadas?p=874132#post874132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I've heard about Dark Eras and the death of Wolf, the Gauntlet seems to be Pangaea shrunk to the size of a dimensional membrane, Wolf's last attempt at separating Flesh from Shadow. I'm pretty much convinced that the Hosts know Wolf might return if Pangaea is recreated, so instinctually destroying the pseudo-remains of Wolf makes a lot of sense, like maggots eating the rotten carcass of their greatest enemy.<br /> <br /> As Hosts grow in power, though, I believe their motivation switch from &quot;Gauntlet messing&quot; to reforming into the great progenitor. They gain intellect and power, and start to understand what they can become and who is their real threat here in this new world: Uratha.<br /> <br /> However, I do agree that Hosts are too &quot;Black and White&quot; antagonists, beings of utter evil that leave little for interpretation. They overlap too much with Spirits, in my view, just a little harder to detect and less prone to become allies. I would like to see an expansion to Hosts, allowing them more complexity, something that really gives you a reason to struggle with the need to eradicate them.<br /> <br /> My two cents on the Cicada: Love the Heat and Sound idea, and maybe you could move them to a shade of grey antagonism, with them being useful to the Hisil ecosystem somehow. Maybe beings that spend millenia asleep under the earth, having to emerge to devour, but also possessing rare knowledge of Rituals or even Gifts that might aid the Uratha. They might have no grudge against Wolf, and be a neutral Host that may, or may not, fuck up your life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that they are really black and white, but that is what makes me love them. In a world where there is shades of grey everywhere ( possibly fifty or more.. I'm so sorry), I like a few enemies that are more &quot;black&quot;, sometimes you just need something to fight and kill that won't create an episode of moral drama theater. Having said that.. for shards who are more intelligent and &quot;whole&quot; I do make them more grey and approachable.. well with shartha like Azlu or Razilu. Beshilu are always frothing, paranoid psychopathic cowards... some just learn how to inspire others to be meat shields so they can pretend to be brave.<br /> <br /> And if you like a more neutral Host, Cinder's Bee Host thread is fucking awesome. Now I can see Cicadas as being neutral.. but only about as neutral as the zerg are when they rush everybody XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 04-26-2016, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T06:55:39-07:00","id":874504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/873199-attack-of-the-cicadas?p=874017#post874017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With the heat manipulation, it reminds me of something that some bees do to fight off intruders in the hive without having to sting them. They grab onto the intruder, enclosing it in a ball of bees. The bees then start to vibrate their wings, heating up the air and effectively cooking the intruder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which shouldn't be bee exclusive for Hosts methinks<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T07:14:28-07:00","id":874513,"title":"","content":"I was going to make cicadas one of the hosts for my australian game, though I wouldn't go with there sound changing to &quot;try to fight off intruders thing&quot;, when the noise is to attract stuff rather than get things away. I was going to have them send out pulses that pull nearby spirits through the gauntlet as it drums, leaving the local spirits disoriented and bleeding essence in the mortal world... It'd also probably leave a rather grisly remnant of it's human victims, leaving what's left of their corpses on the top of buildings and halfway up trees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T07:28:26-07:00","id":874523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/873199-attack-of-the-cicadas?p=874504#post874504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which shouldn't be bee exclusive for Hosts methinks</div> </div> </div> </div>hardyhardyhar","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T14:53:19-07:00","id":874911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/873199-attack-of-the-cicadas?p=874513#post874513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was going to make cicadas one of the hosts for my australian game, though I wouldn't go with there sound changing to &amp;quot;try to fight off intruders thing&amp;quot;, when the noise is to attract stuff rather than get things away. I was going to have them send out pulses that pull nearby spirits through the gauntlet as it drums, leaving the local spirits disoriented and bleeding essence in the mortal world... It'd also probably leave a rather grisly remnant of it's human victims, leaving what's left of their corpses on the top of buildings and halfway up trees.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this idea <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T06:00:14-07:00","id":876540,"title":"","content":"See latest <b>Supernatural </b>episode - &quot;The Chitters&quot; - it's basically Cicadas Claimed 101. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T11:08:59-07:00","id":878875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/873199-attack-of-the-cicadas?p=874132#post874132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> However, I do agree that Hosts are too &quot;Black and White&quot; antagonists, beings of utter evil that leave little for interpretation. They overlap too much with Spirits, in my view, just a little harder to detect and less prone to become allies. I would like to see an expansion to Hosts, allowing them more complexity, something that really gives you a reason to struggle with the need to eradicate them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, perhaps this helps the whole black and white nature of the Hosts seem more reasonable, if you like art. Note that these are not my words, but I do agree with them.<br /> <br /> &quot;When composing a black and white drawing, or charcoal etching, or whatever, the thing that gives the image Depth is the degree of difference you can create between the bright points and the dark points. If everything is grey, the piece lacks contrast, looks more like a sketch than an image, and ultimately cannot catch the eye due to its sheer lack of detail.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think that captures the schism between Hosts and Uratha pretty well I think. Sure nuance is great for a singular antagonist, but when the species is mostly grey ( in a moral sense).. you lose sight of what lines need to remain uncrossed and when to step up and say &quot;enough is enough, we're not letting you body jack people any more&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T19:09:01-07:00","id":886856,"title":"","content":"Not everything in the world (of darkness) has to be some shade of gray, the occasional glimpse of black or white can be good for the overall perspective. Sometimes, the pack just needs something to hunt down, dig their claws and fangs in, and vent a bit of their rage, without any moral dilemmas attached.<br /> <br /> Really, I imagine cicada hosts swarming in a locus and <i>vibrating</i> the gauntlet, shaking the the boundary between flesh and spirit with that droning mating call.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I forgot to mention what all that vibrating does to the gauntlet, didn't I?<br /> <br /> I picture it knocking things loose from their spiritual reflections. Roads in the shadow shift like diverted rivers, an office building begins leaning to one side in the flesh, while its spiritual refection remains as upright as ever. As the mating call attracts more hosts, and the swarm gains new 'singers', the vibrations become even stronger, and farther reaching, until they finally lead to something resembling an earthquake that knocks things across the gauntlet.<br /> <br /> The hosts don't care about the upheaval their song causes, they sing for another reason. Maybe it's just to attract more of their kind, and prepare mating grounds, maybe it's something else, maybe singing the song is their goal in and of itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":2598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","user":"Gryphon's Feather","date":". 05-09-2016, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T21:17:04-07:00","id":886943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryphon's Feather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/873199-attack-of-the-cicadas?p=886856#post886856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not everything in the world (of darkness) has to be some shade of gray, the occasional glimpse of black or white can be good for the overall perspective. Sometimes, the pack just needs something to hunt down, dig their claws and fangs in, and vent a bit of their rage, without any moral dilemmas attached.<br /> <br /> Really, I imagine cicada hosts swarming in a locus and <i>vibrating</i> the gauntlet, shaking the the boundary between flesh and spirit with that droning mating call.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I forgot to mention what all that vibrating does to the gauntlet, didn't I?<br /> <br /> I picture it knocking things loose from their spiritual reflections. Roads in the shadow shift like diverted rivers, an office building begins leaning to one side in the flesh, while its spiritual refection remains as upright as ever. As the mating call attracts more hosts, and the swarm gains new 'singers', the vibrations become even stronger, and farther reaching, until they finally lead to something resembling an earthquake that knocks things across the gauntlet.<br /> <br /> The hosts don't care about the upheaval their song causes, they sing for another reason. Maybe it's just to attract more of their kind, and prepare mating grounds, maybe it's something else, maybe singing the song is their goal in and of itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh. I am liking this tidbit. Really cool, and very thematic,<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}